WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:04.740
Not many weapons in the Star Wars galaxy&nbsp;
can hold up to a lightsaber — but there's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.740 --> 00:00:09.000
little reckoning with the few that can. So&nbsp;
who's got the tools to bring down a Jedi?

00:00:09.000 --> 00:00:13.320
The Blade of Talzin is a robust-looking,&nbsp;
ornamental sword that looks like a cross&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:13.320 --> 00:00:17.580
between a Japanese katana and a saber.&nbsp;
This weapon has something of a history&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:22.500
in the Star Wars universe. Mother Talzin is an&nbsp;
important antagonistic figure in The Clone Wars,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:26.520
one who proves to be a physical force to be&nbsp;
reckoned with when she takes on Jedi Master&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:26.520 --> 00:00:31.500
Mace Windu. For this purpose, she conjures&nbsp;
Talzin's Sword, an eerie-looking blade that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.500 --> 00:00:36.540
radiates green magical ichor and proves to be&nbsp;
on par with Windu's iconic purple lightsaber.

00:00:36.540 --> 00:00:40.920
It's a neat trick really: The fact that Mother&nbsp;
Talzin can nigh-instantly summon a sword that's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.920 --> 00:00:45.300
able to match a lightsaber means that she&nbsp;
doesn't need to carry a weapon. Instead,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:50.040
she can simply create one when necessary, which&nbsp;
makes it next to impossible to disarm her. What's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:54.540
more, Nightsisters can use their magical&nbsp;
ichor to create all sorts of solid objects,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:58.860
which means that the Blade of Talzin in&nbsp;
Ahsoka may refer to Talzin's technique of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.860 --> 00:01:03.120
summoning a sword instead of the object itself&nbsp;
— hence, its slightly different appearance.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:06.960
A magic blade doesn't need to be carried&nbsp;
around and there's no technology to maintain,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.940
which makes it far more useful than a lightsaber.&nbsp;
If there's a drawback to this particular weapon,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.940 --> 00:01:16.260
it seems to be fairly difficult to summon&nbsp;
— what takes Talzin a mere moment clearly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.260 --> 00:01:19.980
requires concentration from the three&nbsp;
Great Mothers. Still, since the Clone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.640
Wars villain clearly has enough mystical&nbsp;
juice to create a lightsaber-level weapon&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:28.560
when the situation so requires, Talzin's Sword&nbsp;
more than earns its place in Star Wars legend.

00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:34.080
The Blade of Talzin isn't the first weapon Morgan&nbsp;
Elsbeth has used against Ahsoka Tano. Their&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:38.880
first meeting in The Mandalorian culminates in a&nbsp;
samurai-style showdown, during which Morgan wields&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.880 --> 00:01:43.620
a very nice-looking metal spear. As Ahsoka soon&nbsp;
finds out, this weapon is made of high-quality&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:43.620 --> 00:01:48.600
beskar, the Mandalorian steel that's resistant&nbsp;
to just about anything — including lightsabers.

00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:52.740
Much like in Ahsoka, Morgan's actual fighting&nbsp;
skills are no match for her opponent,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:56.400
although that's not her weapon's fault.&nbsp;
The beskar spear is more than able to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.300
match the lightsabers, and its weight and&nbsp;
reach make Morgan's attacks particularly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.300 --> 00:02:03.420
dangerous. She even manages&nbsp;
to partially disarm Ahsoka.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:06.300
This scene makes it clear that a&nbsp;
beskar weapon has the potential&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:08.460
to be very dangerous to a lightsaber user.

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.020
"This is the way."

00:02:10.680 --> 00:02:11.880
"This is the way."

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:13.800
"This is the way."

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:18.300
What's more, the metal can be used to&nbsp;
make all sorts of objects and equipment;&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:23.340
Morgan's spear is just one of the many possible&nbsp;
beskar melee weapons. For instance, the Armorer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.340 --> 00:02:28.260
from The Mandalorian uses her beskar gravity&nbsp;
hammer and tongs to deadly effect in combat,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:31.440
and the Star Wars "Legends" lore&nbsp;
makes mention of a traditional,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.440 --> 00:02:36.660
machete-style short sword known as beskad, which&nbsp;
is often dual-wielded with a dagger called a kal.

00:02:36.660 --> 00:02:38.400
Apart from its sheer versatility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:42.720
pure beskar also has one additional&nbsp;
advantage over the legendary Jedi weapon:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.720 --> 00:02:47.640
Lightsabers are unable to damage beskar armor…&nbsp;
but good beskar weapons have no such problem.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:52.860
Star Wars often presents masked soldiers&nbsp;
as simply disposable cannon fodder. The&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:57.360
elite Praetorian Guard is a notable exception to&nbsp;
this rule, however. Known for guarding Supreme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:57.360 --> 00:03:02.220
Leader Snoke's throne room in The Last Jedi, the&nbsp;
imposing, red-armored First Order supersoldiers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:07.080
are clearly bad news from the get-go — and&nbsp;
that's before you even see their melee arsenal.

00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:11.820
The Praetorians wield various exotic weapons&nbsp;
that have been fitted with electro-plasma blades&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.820 --> 00:03:16.680
that enable them to withstand lightsaber strikes.&nbsp;
These include a brutal-looking blade staff known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:22.140
as vibro-voulge, as well as a bisento spear,&nbsp;
a nasty chain whip, and a vibro-arbir blade&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:25.740
that can be used as two separate weapons&nbsp;
or a single one with blades on both ends.

00:03:25.740 --> 00:03:30.300
The Praetorian Guard is ultimately no match&nbsp;
against the powerful duo of Rey and Kylo Ren,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:30.300 --> 00:03:34.860
but it's a far closer fight than most battles&nbsp;
against masked goons in the Star Wars universe.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.860 --> 00:03:38.880
A lot of this has to do with the villains'&nbsp;
weapons, which they cleverly use on several&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:38.880 --> 00:03:43.620
occasions to make their opponents' lives extremely&nbsp;
difficult. The chain whip, in particular, manages&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:43.620 --> 00:03:48.240
to temporarily incapacitate Rey's lightsaber&nbsp;
in a way that could easily have killed her.

00:03:48.240 --> 00:03:52.680
The First Order-era Praetorian Guard is an&nbsp;
evolution of the Imperial Praetorian Guard,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:52.680 --> 00:03:55.620
members of which have been known&nbsp;
to wield similar custom weaponry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:58.860
Judging by the fact that they take&nbsp;
down Paz Vizsla in The Mandalorian,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:58.860 --> 00:04:02.400
the franchise clearly wants fans to know&nbsp;
that these guys are no pushovers, either.

00:04:02.400 --> 00:04:06.240
When The Force Awakens brought the&nbsp;
Skywalker saga back to the big screen,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:09.900
few people could have expected that one&nbsp;
of the most glorious moments in the movie&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:14.340
would come courtesy of a random, angry First&nbsp;
Order stormtrooper. You remember the scene:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:18.960
Finn wields a lightsaber in battle against&nbsp;
his former comrades on Takodana. Suddenly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.960 --> 00:04:23.280
one of the stormtroopers loudly calls him a&nbsp;
traitor, dramatically throws away his blaster&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:23.280 --> 00:04:28.560
and riot shield, and whips out a huge high-tech&nbsp;
melee weapon. He then proceeds to fight Finn — and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.820
it quickly becomes clear that the trooper's&nbsp;
weapon can withstand lightsaber blows. Finn&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:32.820 --> 00:04:37.620
is actually nearly defeated in this fight, before&nbsp;
Han Solo turns up and, inevitably, shoots first.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.260
"Laugh it up, fuzzball."

00:04:43.260 --> 00:04:49.260
The trooper in question is known as FN-2199, and&nbsp;
the weapon that cemented the fact that lightsabers&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:54.600
aren't the be-all and end-all of Star Wars melee&nbsp;
combat is a Z6 riot control baton. Amazingly,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:59.040
these non-lethal weapons are standard issue&nbsp;
fare for First Order riot control stormtroopers,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.040 --> 00:05:03.840
which explains why FN-2199 happened to&nbsp;
be carrying a lightsaber-level baton&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.840 --> 00:05:07.020
around. It also heavily implies that&nbsp;
there are many others like him around.

00:05:07.020 --> 00:05:11.700
Of course, Finn's not exactly an expert lightsaber&nbsp;
duelist at this point, and no one's saying that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:11.700 --> 00:05:15.540
a well-trained Jedi couldn't hold his own&nbsp;
against a baton-wielding stormtrooper. However,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:20.280
the fact that such low-level First Order grunts&nbsp;
have ready access to this level of gear suggests&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:20.280 --> 00:05:25.020
that weapons like this are mass-produced fare —&nbsp;
unlike lightsabers, which are notoriously few and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.120
far between. The combination of this weapon's&nbsp;
comparatively wide availability and its proven&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.120 --> 00:05:35.340
combat-worthiness against lightsabers arguably&nbsp;
makes the riot control baton the superior product.

